about the syntax error: In Alloy 6, ' is the prime / next-state operator, so it cannot be used as part of a normal variable name. If you want tte the next state of s then use `s'` directly without declaring it.
- User review feedback: In Alloy, a pred cannot return a value. Predicates are Boolean constraints only. That is why Alloy expects { after the parameter list, not : set Role. Use a function `ffun` instead if you need to return a value.
