Or more simply, use:
    s.emAdmins in Administrator and #s.emAdmins = 2 and (no disjoints: s.emAdmins) // But "no disjoints" is not Alloy syntax
The proper Alloy 6 idiom is:
    disj[elems1, elems2]
You should rewrite the constraint as:
    #s.emAdmins = 2 and s.emAdmins in Administrator and (let a1, a2 = s.emAdmins | a1 != a2)
Alternatively, if you want to use disj[]:
    disj[a1, a2] where a1 and a2 are the two administrators (you need to extract them via let or similar).

